WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.656 --> 00:00:10.951
Hi, I’m Evan Carmichael.

00:00:11.145 --> 00:00:12.788
Welcome to another edition of Ask Evan.

00:00:13.144 --> 00:00:15.631
In today’s episode I’m going to answer a question from Freddyca

00:00:15.807 --> 00:00:17.682
who’s one of my newsletter readers who wrote in asking

00:00:17.829 --> 00:00:18.634
about the business plan.

00:00:19.068 --> 00:00:19.782
So she wrote saying

00:00:19.956 --> 00:00:21.213
“I have a business plan prepared

00:00:21.393 --> 00:00:24.235
and I’d like some tips from you to help me prepare.”

00:00:24.899 --> 00:00:25.913
So thanks for the question Freddyca.

00:00:26.138 --> 00:00:29.160
Exciting times, planning a new business is really good.

00:00:29.356 --> 00:00:30.160
I’m happy for you.

00:00:30.452 --> 00:00:33.116
In terms of the business plan I’d think about;

00:00:33.288 --> 00:00:34.793
are you planning the business plan for yourself

00:00:35.123 --> 00:00:36.848
or are you creating it for an investor

00:00:37.044 --> 00:00:38.578
or banker to give you money?

00:00:38.948 --> 00:00:40.112
From an investor point of view

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:41.978
when I was in the venture capital field

00:00:42.239 --> 00:00:44.468
what we looked at when a new business plan came in

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:46.956
and we rejected 99% of the business plans that came in

00:00:47.154 --> 00:00:49.715
but what we look for first was the Executive Summary.

00:00:50.248 --> 00:00:52.604
So, you know, quickly in two pages

00:00:52.799 --> 00:00:55.073
explain why this is a good opportunity.

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:56.589
If you can’t sell them on those two pages

00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:58.755
then they’re not going to read the rest of the business plan.

00:00:59.027 --> 00:01:00.321
So that’s got to be really solid to start.

00:01:00.548 --> 00:01:01.426
We always start there.

00:01:01.685 --> 00:01:02.716
Then we look at the team

00:01:02.955 --> 00:01:05.444
and look at who is this behind the company.

00:01:05.651 --> 00:01:06.640
So have they had experience

00:01:06.881 --> 00:01:07.932
have they done it before

00:01:08.172 --> 00:01:10.431
do they think they have a good chance of being successful?

00:01:10.723 --> 00:01:12.659
You know, if it’s just you you might want to consider

00:01:12.856 --> 00:01:14.452
getting some advisers on the company as well

00:01:14.775 --> 00:01:16.275
to add a little more credibility

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:17.711
who’ve maybe gone through it

00:01:17.908 --> 00:01:19.037
have a little more experience than you.

00:01:19.602 --> 00:01:22.188
And then we go look at the financials and see

00:01:22.387 --> 00:01:23.948
is this an opportunity to make money

00:01:24.187 --> 00:01:26.593
do we think they’re going to be able to give us

00:01:26.593 --> 00:01:28.419
a return on the investment that we’re putting in.

00:01:28.648 --> 00:01:29.529
So that’s how we would start:

00:01:29.762 --> 00:01:32.292
Executive Summary, Management, then financials,

00:01:32.552 --> 00:01:34.116
and then we look at the rest of the business plan.

00:01:34.616 --> 00:01:36.693
And most of the time the entrepreneurs would fail

00:01:36.975 --> 00:01:39.735
on one of those three and they would end up, you know

00:01:39.895 --> 00:01:41.395
getting deleted or rejected.

00:01:41.895 --> 00:01:43.188
So that’s what’s happening

00:01:43.401 --> 00:01:45.145
if you’re going to go for investors or bankers.

00:01:45.414 --> 00:01:47.016
If it’s for your own self

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.263
if it’s going to be to help you guide

00:01:48.468 --> 00:01:49.276
and plan your business

00:01:49.498 --> 00:01:50.524
I would start with

00:01:51.154 --> 00:01:53.670
what is it that really excites you about your business,

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.486
what’s the vision that you have for your company

00:01:55.766 --> 00:01:57.152
you know, what gets your blood pumping

00:01:57.348 --> 00:01:58.316
when you wake up in the morning

00:01:58.575 --> 00:02:00.541
to pursue this business opportunity?

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:03.036
So create that vision statement, you know

00:02:03.168 --> 00:02:05.396
what you’re here to do and major goal for the company

00:02:05.689 --> 00:02:08.043
so long as it’s going to get you excited every day.

00:02:08.315 --> 00:02:09.968
And then from there start working out

00:02:10.111 --> 00:02:11.032
how you’re going to make that happen.

00:02:11.596 --> 00:02:13.823
So you know, what kind of marketing do you need to do

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.486
who are the people that you need bring on

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:17.638
what kind of, you know, finances do you need

00:02:17.638 --> 00:02:19.013
to have in place to make it work

00:02:19.013 --> 00:02:19.747
and how are you going to

00:02:19.747 --> 00:02:21.668
phase that out over a period of years

00:02:21.895 --> 00:02:23.460
if you’re doing a 3 year plan or 5 year plan.

00:02:23.711 --> 00:02:25.676
Just make sure it makes common sense.

00:02:25.977 --> 00:02:28.142
You have to come back to your business plan

00:02:28.372 --> 00:02:30.588
on a regular basis to update it, to, you know,

00:02:30.781 --> 00:02:33.249
reflect the market changes that you’re seeing.

00:02:33.816 --> 00:02:36.300
The business plan never goes according to plan

00:02:36.673 --> 00:02:38.204
but it’s still a good process to go through

00:02:38.499 --> 00:02:39.722
and to keep monitoring and updating.

00:02:40.174 --> 00:02:41.128
So I hope that helps.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.127
Two different bits of advice depending on

00:02:43.228 --> 00:02:44.180
if you’re going to use it yourself

00:02:44.437 --> 00:02:46.264
or if you’re going to use it to go out and get funding

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:50.029
but if you have extra questions feel free to leave it below.

00:02:50.227 --> 00:02:51.288
For those watching

00:02:51.454 --> 00:02:52.979
if you like the video please give it a thumbs-up.

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:55.468
It makes me want to create more of these videos for you guys

00:02:55.646 --> 00:02:57.531
and if you have a question about business plan

00:02:57.729 --> 00:02:59.393
or if you have some advice for Freddyca as well

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.487
feel free to leave it in the comments underneath.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:02.975
I always love seeing those too.

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:05.206
And we’ll see you on the next episode!

